{"name":"California Chamois","hex":"#e6b76c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chamois","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A short-horned goat antelope native to mountainous terrain in southern Europe; Rupicapra rupicapra.","Ellipsis of chamois leather (“soft pliable leather originally made from the skin of chamois (nowadays the hides of deer, sheep, and other species of goat are alternatively used)”)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Chamois-colored."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chamois"}],"entries":[{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California","wikidata":"Q99"},{"title":"Chamois","blocks":[{"text":"The chamois, or Alpine chamois, is a species of goat-antelope native to mountainous parts of Europe and Western Asia, from the Pyrenees and the Cantabrian Mountain Range, the Alps, the Apennines, the Dinarides, the Tatra to the Carpathian Mountains, the Balkan Mountains, the Rila–Rhodope massif, Pindus, the northeastern mountains of Turkey, and the Caucasus. It has also been introduced to the South Island of New Zealand. Some subspecies of chamois are strictly protected in the EU under the European Habitats Directive."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/064_Wild_Chamois_Parc_r%C3%A9gional_Chasseral_Photo_by_Giles_Laurent.jpg/330px-064_Wild_Chamois_Parc_r%C3%A9giona